,"`",")",";","}","}","}","}"]},"context":{"before":"382431816eb816f3"}},"payload":{"text":"Load the site's extensions and the ones `?extension=` names; resolves once each one is in the editor (or failed to\nload, and said so).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:00.619Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:00.619Z"}
{"id":"c6b9cec5-a593-43b3-b15b-6a0785d404f5","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"ecf07076a9107705","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/extensions.ts","baseline":{"blob":"71531fb2d64093766d282c09696f35f13aa1a312","start":4062,"end":4179},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","root","=","new","URL","(","location",".","pathname",".","slice","(","0",",","location",".","pathname",".","indexOf","(","\"","/__vscode__/","\"",")","+","1",")","||","\"","/","\"",",","location",".","href",")"]},"context":{"before":"cc9ed3191f35f6d0","after":"083a6c7230ae29de"}},"payload":{"text":"The site's root: the workbench is at <root>/__vscode__/host.html.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:01.796Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:01.796Z"}
{"id":"daa89366-1ee1-4f71-bab2-1ab65520956d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e46e22f049b9d08c","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/extensions.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9287516d611fd0bd126298afd0b288aa8aca004f","start":0,"end":40},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","*","as","vscodeApi","from","\"","vscode","\""]},"context":{"after":"d116c123373a14a2"}},"payload":{"text":"Every extension loads from a folder: its package.json, its `browser` entry, and the files its manifest's `files`\nlists (a worker it starts, a tsserver plugin's package, a webview's script) — each registered at its path in the\nfolder, so the extension opens it as `extensionUri`'s (registerExtensionFolder). The editor's own are built into\n`extensions/<name>/` (build.ts, bundledExtension) and registered by workbench-entry; extensions from outside the\neditor — an interpreter or a code renderer built from editor-contrib's template (contrib/README.md) — the same way,\nby URL: the URL its package.json is at or the folder it's in. Two lists name those: the site's own `extensions.json`\nbeside its index.html, its URLs relative to the site (a site that's the editor with extensions of its own:\neditor-contrib's is the editor's tarball, its extension added), and the page's `?extension=`s (one served from\nanywhere, while it's developed — reloading the editor as it's rebuilt: `followChanges`). Their code runs in the web\nworker extension host, with the access every extension there has.\n\nThe extension host's CSP takes its code from https, or http on `localhost:*` / `127.0.0.1:*` (one under\ndevelopment) — not a `*.localhost` name.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:07.759Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:07.759Z"}
{"id":"ea2c9ce2-dc41-464a-9fc0-cf9ffd6a603a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"70163612d1656236","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/extensions.ts","baseline":{"blob":"58fc5656a0057fb74f57b5ab91c2ba51b565e015","start":3261,"end":3671},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","followChanges","(","base",":","URL",")",":","void","{","if","(","base",".","protocol","!==","\"","http:","\"",")","{","return",";","}","const","changes","=","new","EventSource","(","new","URL","(","\"","__changes","\"",",","base",")",")",";","let","opened","=","false",";","changes",".","addEventListener","(","\"","open","\"",",","(",")","=>","{","opened","=","true",";","}",")",";","changes",".","addEventListener","(","\"","error","\"",",","(",")","=>","{","if","(","!","opened",")","{","changes",".","close","(",")",";","}","}",")",";","changes",".","addEventListener","(","\"","change","\"",",","(",")","=>","{","window",".","top","?.","location",".","reload","(",")",";","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"ddde9c95d2482058","after":"382431816eb816f3"}},"payload":{"text":"An extension being developed on this machine (editor-contrib's `npm run dev`): the editor reloads when its change\nstream (`__changes`) says it was rebuilt. A server without one is let be — the stream is closed, not retried.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:04.153Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:04.153Z"}
